Organization = {Conf \& Labs Evaluat Forum Assoc},
Abstract = {The Hate and Morality (HAMoR) submission for the Profiling Hate Speech
   Spreaders on Twitter task at PAN 2021 ranked as the 19th position - over
   67 participating teams - according to the averaged accuracy value of
   73\% over the two languages - English (62\%) and Spanish (84\%). The
   method proposed four types of features for inferring users attitudes
   just from the text in their messages: HS detection, users morality,
   named entities, and communicative behaviour. In this paper, since the
   test set is now available, we were able to analyse false negative and
   false positive prediction with the aim of shed more light on the hate
   speech spreading phenomena. Furthermore, we fine-tuned the features
   based on users morality and named entities showing that semantic
   resources could help in facing Hate Speech Spreaders detection on
   Twitter.},
